# Per-device topic access, for the hardened configuration.
#
# Signaling topics are signaling/<node_id>/<message type>. A device must
# publish to its peers' topics and subscribe to its own. Mosquitto cannot bind
# a topic to a device's node_id, so the split is: everyone may publish, nobody
# may subscribe outside their own subtree.
#
# Rename this to `acl`, point `acl_file` at it, and replace the usernames and
# node_ids below. A node_id is shown on the "My Device" card in
# Settings > Sync, and is 43 characters of base64url.

# Publishing to a peer is how pairing works at all, so it cannot be restricted
# to known peers up front. A forged message is useless: it will not carry a
# valid signature.
pattern write signaling/+/+

# Reading is the part that matters: without these lines any authenticated
# client could subscribe to signaling/# and watch every pairing on the broker.
# One block per device.
user laptop
topic read signaling/REPLACE-WITH-LAPTOP-NODE-ID/+

user phone
topic read signaling/REPLACE-WITH-PHONE-NODE-ID/+
